        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(find): prevent recursive re-entry in child kill via sentinel guard (#98961)",
        "body": "Fixes #98961.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nIn `find.ts`, `child.on(\"error\")` only called `cleanup()` (which closed readline), while `child.on(\"close\")` called both `cleanup()` and `stopChild?.()`. On spawn failure or certain error paths, the child process was not killed — leaving a potential orphan.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nTwo changes with a safety sentinel:\n\n1. **`cleanup()` now calls `stopChild?.()`** — so both error and close handlers stop the child symmetrically.\n\n2. **`stopChild` uses a `stopChildKilling` sentinel** — prevents recursive re-entry if `child.kill()` triggers Node's `error` event before `settle` clears the hook.\n\nThe direct fix proposed in #98854 (calling `stopChild` in the error handler without a sentinel) risks recursive kill — if `child.kill()` emits another `error` event, the handler re-enters, calls `kill()` again, and potentially loops. The sentinel prevents this.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo user-visible behavior change. Fixes an edge case where a spawn-failing fd find could leave an orphan child process.\n\n## Evidence\n\n**Real environment tested:** local OpenClaw source checkout, Node v24.13.1, PR head.\n\n**Proof — focused regression test exercises the real `createFindToolDefinition` with mocked child process (same pattern as merged #99446):**\n\n```\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/sessions/tools/find.test.ts --run\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  3 passed (3)\n```\n\nThe new test \"stops child on spawn error and prevents recursive kill via sentinel\":\n1. Creates the real `createFindToolDefinition(\"/workspace\")` \n2. Mocks `spawn` and `ensureTool(\"fd\")` (same pattern as `find.fd.test.ts` from merged #99446)\n3. Triggers `child.emit(\"error\", new Error(\"ENOENT\"))` — the spawn failure path\n4. Asserts `expect(result).rejects.toThrow(\"Failed to run fd\")` — error → cleanup → stopChild → kill → settle\n5. Asserts `expect(child.killMock).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(1)` — child was killed\n6. Triggers `child.emit(\"close\", null, \"SIGTERM\")` — Node's post-kill close event\n7. Asserts `expect(child.killMock).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(1)` — sentinel prevented recursive second kill\n\n```\n$ npx oxlint src/agents/sessions/tools/find.ts src/agents/sessions/tools/find.test.ts\n→ exit 0\n```\n\n**Observed result after fix:** On spawn error, `cleanup()` calls `stopChild?.()` → `child.kill()`. When Node then emits `close`, `cleanup()` is called again but `stopChildKilling` is `true`, so the sentinel returns without a second `kill()`. No orphan process, no recursive re-entry.\n\n**What was not tested:** Live end-to-end with a real `fd` binary (fd is not installed in this environment). The test exercises the full production tool path through `createFindToolDefinition` with a mocked child process — same pattern as the already-merged `find.fd.test.ts` from #99446 (diamond lobster).\n\n## Regression Test Plan\n\n- `$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/sessions/tools/find.test.ts --run` — **1 passed, 3 tests passed** (2 existing + 1 new sentinel test)\n- `$ npx oxlint src/agents/sessions/tools/find.ts src/agents/sessions/tools/find.test.ts` — **exit 0**\n- `$ git diff --stat` — **2 files, +68/-3**\n\n## Root Cause\n\nIn `createFindToolDefinition`, the `error` handler called `cleanup()` (rl.close only) but not `stopChild?.()`. The `close` handler called both. A direct fix adding `stopChild?.()` to the error handler risks recursive re-entry if `child.kill()` emits an `error` event before `settle` runs. The fix uses a `stopChildKilling` sentinel boolean — set before `child.kill()`, checked at entry — to prevent re-entry.\n\nAI-assisted: Claude Opus 4.8",
        "branch": "fix/fd-find-error-stopchild-98961",
